## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates cross-tenant governance, certificate-based service principal authentication, and automated credential rotation at scale—essential competencies for enterprise SaaS integrations.

## Key Concepts
- Certificate rotation with Key Vault integration, including automatic expiration monitoring and secret versioning
- Least-privilege Graph permissions configured for multi-tenant automation scenarios
- Sandbox validation environments, comprehensive auditing across Azure AD and partner tenants
- Managed Identity usage for secure, credential-less certificate retrieval

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: fetch cert from Key Vault and prepare Graph app update
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');

async function getCertificate() {
  const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
  const client = new SecretClient('https://your-vault.vault.azure.net', credential);
  const certificate = await client.getSecret('partner-sp-certificate');
  return certificate.value;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-world governance for privileged access, focusing on JIT, approvals, and audit trail at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
- Just-In-Time (JIT) elevation
- Approval workflows and MFA enforcement
- Activation windows, justification, auto-revocation
- Audit trails, post-activation reviews, sandbox testing

## Code Example
```javascript
async function requestPimActivation(userId, roleId, durationHrs, justification){
  const token = await getAadToken();
  const res = await fetch(`https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/privilegedRoles/${roleId}/activate`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type':'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ principalId: userId, duration: `PT${durationHrs}H`, reason: justification, notifyUsers: true })
  });
  return res.json();
}
```

